# Conventional Commits: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   type    feat | fix | docs | style | refactor | perf | test | build | ci | chore | revert
#   scope   changed module, "/" for nesting, e.g. drv/usb, example/rt_device/uart
#   subject one line, imperative, lowercase, no trailing period
#
# Body (optional): why the change is needed and how it works, wrapped at 72 columns.
# Lead with the point: the problem when the body reports one, otherwise the decision;
# name a file or function only when the reader needs it to follow that. A body that
# tours the diff adds nothing to it.
# Put the problem paragraph before the resolution paragraph, in separate paragraphs; each must be
# identifiable from its first sentence without a `Problem:`/`Resolution:` prefix.
# Breaking change: write type(scope)!: ... and add a "BREAKING CHANGE: ..." footer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<type>(<scope>): short imperative summary

# Explain why the change is needed.
#
# Then what the change does about it.

ext-redmine: #id, REDMINE-id
